Now I laugh and tell them about a confusing Saturday.
It was a cold Saturday morning that first winter.
I wanted to walk down to the harbour.
Nina gave me the route beforehand.
On the way I heard a street musician.
He played the guitar beautifully.
I stopped and listened for a long time.
Then I completely forgot Nina's route.
I walked into a narrow side street.
There were only small, quiet houses.
Suddenly I got completely lost.
Ahead of me walked a young woman with a little dog.
The dog looked exactly like our Lola.
"Excuse me, I am looking for the harbour," I said.
She kindly pointed me back towards the square.
I thanked her and found the right way.
In the end I reached the water.
My brother Diego laughs loudly on the screen.
It was a silly mistake, but a good memory.
